# Landing page builds

When the user provides `Type: Landing Page`, `Slug:`, and full copy:

1. Immediately create `app/<slug>/page.tsx`. If Write fails because the file exists, stop. Do not overwrite.
2. Use this boilerplate from memory only: metadata, canonical, Open Graph, Service schema, Nav, LandingPageCTA after the H1, article content, Related Reading, FinalCTA, Footer.
3. Preserve the supplied copy and headings.
4. Do not search the repository.
5. Do not check the sitemap.
6. Do not inspect other landing pages.
7. Do not run terminal commands, build, test, lint, commit, or push.
8. Do not update `sitemap.ts` or `blogSpecialtyLinks.tsx` in this turn.
9. Stop immediately after the page file is written.

Touch only `app/<slug>/page.tsx`.

Do not think. Do not plan. Do not reply first. Do not grep, search, read sitemap, inspect other pages, verify duplicates, lint, test, or build.

Reply with only:
- New page created: [slug]
- Files changed: [list]
- Existing content overwritten: No
- Committed/pushed: No

## Page file

Boilerplate from memory only. Do not open other landing pages.

Article: `section-container max-w-[720px]`, `blog-prose`. After the H1, before article copy, include `<LandingPageCTA specialty="[Title Case Specialty]" />`. Related Reading via `getBlogPostsBySpecialty` (max 5). Preserve user H2s. No em dashes. Attorney tone. Closing H2 **Find a [X] Expert Witness** plus `Start an expert witness search` → `/expert-witness-search` plus `<FinalCTA />` after Related Reading.

`SpecialtyLink` only if the slug is already known. If unsure, leave plain text. No standalone nursing specialty. Insurance stays plain text.

Known cross-links: `/expert-witness-search`, `/blog/when-your-case-needs-two-expert-witnesses`, `/blog/qualifying-an-expert-witness`, `/medical-expert-witness`, `/expert-witness/engineering`.

Never touch `/freight-broker-expert-witness`.
